  "lineage": "Vietnamese cải lương (\"renovated theatre\") southern-Vietnamese popular-and-classical theatrical tradition emerging in 1917 in Mekong Delta region as a modernization of the older hát bội classical-court-opera tradition, incorporating Western-style spoken dialogue and naturalistic staging while retaining the đờn ca tài tử southern-amateur-music instrumental tradition as musical foundation. The genre flourished through the colonial-period Mekong Delta and post-1945 Saigon as the dominant southern Vietnamese popular-theatre form. Performance integrates đàn tranh sixteen-string zither, đàn bầu one-string monochord, đàn nguyệt moon-lute, and đàn tỳ bà pear-lute with stylized melodic-recitative vocal-narrative content.",
